#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513020} :activity/id #uuid "b76674c1-c7dc-52f4-97ac-9dbbe620f1e7" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049896 :topic/id #uuid "1c8e94f0-f686-5ab0-b88e-99e6f26eaf54" :topic/math-academy-id 3232} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512967 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512886 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11fb2908-cb3b-5ce4-b240-d1cd6a0c0e4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512138}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512138} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dde5664-1551-5800-8729-df181a92b19e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512767} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbc110d3-28af-5d56-a411-f77e3b06512b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512709}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512709} :answer-field/id #uuid "65909c4d-3bfc-57f3-90ff-59677c9e4afb" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512782} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "297fb137-5002-574b-b9ad-9272c0657eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512193}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512193} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a05b26b-fbd9-504f-b92b-f99d4bfac354" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512806} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52b6abc5-a440-5ffe-a843-31eb841d760a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512282}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512282} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2187910-c471-5e05-bbb3-c1123deb8a70" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4d0a8858-fa20-5f8a-859e-5ff864dcdd44" :question/math-academy-id "q-332402" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{6}{s}-\\frac{2}{s-4},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{3}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-4}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{4t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{6}{s}-\\frac{2}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & =6{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}-2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & =6\\cdot 1-2{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & =6-2{e}^{4t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & =3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & =3+{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6-2{e}^{4t} \\\\ 3+{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "26340763-1380-5c53-9b3f-a306a2619910" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513017}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512995 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512949 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df62ff71-4774-53f9-b7fc-ad0d27a68300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3s-10}{(s-1)(s-4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512636}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512636} :answer-field/id #uuid "695e84fb-9997-5022-b11a-2cd4e22db019" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e1726d67-859b-50b6-a736-a3033ae62d0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-331948" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(2s-9)}{(s-1)(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-4=2{X}_{1}(s)-2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-3=-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-2){X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)=4 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s)+(s-3){X}_{2}(s)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=3-(s-3){X}_{2}(s).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-2)[3-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)]+2{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ 3(s-2)-[(s-2)(s-3)-2]{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-5s+4){X}_{2}(s) & =4-3(s-2) \\\\ -(s-1)(s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =-3s+10 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3s-10}{(s-1)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =3-(s-3){X}_{2}(s) \\\\  & =3-(s-3)\\cdot \\frac{3s-10}{(s-1)(s-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(s-1)(s-4)-(s-3)(3s-10)}{(s-1)(s-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4s-18}{(s-1)(s-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(2s-9)}{(s-1)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(2s-9)}{(s-1)(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3s-10}{(s-1)(s-4)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "65a90e25-be65-5cd0-8609-0b9b0c234c64" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513011}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513011 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512957 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d847229-96cd-5ffd-a231-2ad72cf800f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512265}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512265} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c8f6e0a-6fd1-5b8e-b6eb-9b1fb0b0fea0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512729} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "792912c3-c77e-5ff3-a071-8f72576c2ac8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512384}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512384} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a030071-4ec4-5adf-89a3-4d7bacf1c66e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512756} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a141d64b-becb-5e33-93ee-ab35b9b1dd5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512474}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512474} :answer-field/id #uuid "54b51ff1-8e69-5b64-be8f-00264cd94dc6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512771} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87aed3d1-a1af-50a1-be6b-24983dbaafd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512414}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512414} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb445a54-016a-5ce1-8c7f-2dbdca7b13f9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fafb126e-2901-5759-82dc-9622ce8bea50" :question/math-academy-id "q-332299" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{3}{s-1},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{2}{s-4}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{4t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3}{s-1}\\} \\\\  & =3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\} \\\\  & =3{e}^{1\\cdot t} \\\\  & =3{e}^{t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{2}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}-2{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-2{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}-2{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a6a0b32e-eb09-5421-a596-3e6fd4b1cd5c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512967}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513017 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305035 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61cae97e-e1cf-5e1a-b4b8-212a90585bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303052}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303052} :answer-field/id #uuid "134108ac-f6ce-5da7-ad51-84bc71a18543" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af54400f-b9f6-5982-9407-f85ff881920b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303536}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303536} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d5e1211-c6d7-5e87-9299-f69543b35e89" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304373} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cbd3de9-8819-58ec-a936-9fa202688522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302832}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302832} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbc227f3-81a3-5cb5-bb5e-0ade1394f95f" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304588} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb0ca108-a376-5088-a942-5cb1c1a219af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303925}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303925} :answer-field/id #uuid "eee805e2-49aa-5088-bab0-02cbf6bbb3dc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7ac0cd29-2f59-5bca-b5ae-84aff2ab783d" :question/math-academy-id "q-332409" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{2s}+\\frac{7}{2(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{3}{2s}-\\frac{7}{2(s-4)}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{4t}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{2s}+\\frac{7}{2(s-4)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+\\frac{7}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1+\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s}-\\frac{7}{2(s-4)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-\\frac{7}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 1-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4t} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4t}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2}\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ce979f69-9765-5453-b829-f640b5b3f02e"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513020 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304963 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16626aab-41b1-50e7-9c88-6b61819c1efb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5s+17}{(s+3)(s-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302601}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302601} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d139cec-a218-57e3-8994-0875af73f1e4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304371} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65d0344f-96cb-5c9d-88a4-f4a5b51f28ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303072}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303072} :answer-field/id #uuid "725a473b-f555-5f6a-b695-caf9bb79a521" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "daf5c29f-5732-5955-b4c0-e9cfb924874e" :question/math-academy-id "q-331940" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=-3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-5=2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns{X}_{1}(s)-1=-3{X}_{1}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{1}{s+3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns{X}_{2}(s)-5=2(\\frac{1}{s+3})+{X}_{2}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{5s+17}{(s+3)(s-1)}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d6c97440-18e1-5786-af73-8f601577d3eb" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512995}}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512092}]}
